CHAPTER I GENERAL PROVISIONS

Article 1 (Purpose) The purpose of this Decree is to prescribe matters mandated by the Act on the Management of Buildings and those necessary for the enforcement thereof.

CHAPTER II ESTABLISHMENT OF FOUNDATION FOR BUILDING MANAGEMENT

Article 2 (Establishment of building life cycle information system) (1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(1)10 of the Act on the Management of Buildings (hereinafter referred to as the "Act") means the following matters: <Amended on Oct. 28, 2021; Aug. 2, 2022>
  1. Results of measures, such as repair and reinforcement, taken under Article 22 of the Act;
  2. Results of evaluation on results of building management inspections under Article 24 of the Act;
  3. Results of reinforcement of fire safety performance under Article 28 of the Act;
  4. Information on permission for or report on dismantlement of buildings under Article 30 of the Act;
  5. Information on report on the commencement of dismantlement works under Article 30-2 of the Act;
  6. Results of on-site inspections under Article 30-4 of the Act;
  7. Other matters publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as deemed necessary for building management.
  (2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 7(3)9 of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on Dec. 1, 2020>
  1. Results of examination of appropriateness of a building management plan and results of measures taken therefor under Article 11(4) and (6) of the Act;
  2. Results of building management inspections under Article 20 of the Act;
  3. Information on regular and occasional inspections and close safety examinations under Articles 16-2 and 16-3 of the High-pressure Gas Safety Control Act;
  4. Information on safety inspection and safety management of small-scale multi-family housing under Articles 33 and 34 of the Multi-family Housing Management Act;
  5. Information on regular inspections, non-periodic inspections, detailed safety inspections, and safety evaluations under Articles 17 and 17-2 of the High-pressure Gas Safety Control Act;
  6. Information on business registration under Article 8 of the Value-Added Tax Act;
  7. Information on fact-finding surveys of unoccupied houses under Article 5 of the Act on Special Cases concerning Unoccupied House or Small-Scale Housing Improvement;
  8. Information on safety inspections for facilities under Article 34-4 of the Social Welfare Services Act;
  9. Information on factory establishment management information system under Article 6-2(1) of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act (limited to the information on factory establishment);
  10. Information on seismic performance assessment under Article 12(3) of the Special Act on the Safety Control and Maintenance of Establishments;
  11. Information on measurement of indoor air quality and report thereon under Articles 12 and 13 of the Indoor Air Quality Control Act;
  12. Information on regular inspections, occasional inspections, precise safety diagnosis, and safety evaluation under Articles 37 and 38 of the Safety Control and Business of Liquefied Petroleum Gas Act;
  13. Information on regular facility inspections under Article 12(2) of the Act on the Safety Control of Children's Play Facilities;
  14. Information on regular check and regular inspection under Article 18 of the Act on the Safety Control of Hazardous Substances;
  15. Information on accreditation of medical institutions under Article 58 of the Medical Service Act;
  16. Information on barrier-free living environment certification under Article 10-2 of the Act on the Guarantee of Convenience Promotion of Persons with Disabilities, Senior Citizens, Pregnant Women and Nursing Mothers;
  17. Information on results of government joint safety inspections and results of measure taken therefor under Article 32 of the Act on the Safety Control of Hazardous Substances;
  18. Administrative information established through the local informatization projects under Article 65 of the Electronic Government Act;
  19. Information on in-depth safety inspection of mechanical parking lots under Article 19-23 of the Parking Lot Act;
  20. Information on certification for seismic buildings under Article 16-3 of the Act on the Preparation for Earthquakes and Volcanic Eruptions;
  21. Information on overall evaluation of training facilities under Article 19-2 of the Youth Activity Promotion Act;
  22. Information on school facilities defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the School Facilities Projects Promotion Act;
  23. Information on safety inspections and full safety examinations of school facilities under Articles 13(1) and 14(1) of the Act on the Safety and Maintenance of Educational Facilities;
  24. Other information publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as deemed necessary.

Article 3 (Disclosure of building life cycle information) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (referring to the head of an autonomous Gu; hereinafter the same shall apply) may disclose the following information from among building life cycle information in accordance with Article 8(1) of the Act in cases of public-use buildings defined in subparagraph 17 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act; provided, matters concerning personal information under subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Personal Information Protection Act shall be excluded:
  1. Building management plans;
  2. Information on building management under Article 10 of the Act;
  3. Results of examination of appropriateness of a building management plan and results of measures taken therefor under Article 11(4) and (6) of the Act;
  4. Results of building management inspection under Article 20 of the Act;
  5. Results of measures, such as repair and reinforcement, taken under Article 22 of the Act;
  6. Evaluation on results of building management inspections under Article 24 of the Act;
  7. Results of reinforcement of fire safety performance under Article 28 of the Act;
  8. Results of dismantlement works of a building under Article 33 of the Act;
  9. Information on energy use and greenhouse gas emissions in buildings under Article 10 of the Green Buildings Construction Support Act.

Article 4 (Building life cycle management register) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 9(1)6 of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where measures, such as restrictions on use, prohibition of use, and dismantlement, under Article 21 of the Act are taken;
  2. Where measures, such as repair and reinforcement, under Article 22(1) of the Act are taken;
  3. Where measures, such as dismantlement, alteration, repair, or prohibition or restriction of the use of buildings under Article 22(2) of the Act are taken;
  4. Where reinforcement of fire safety performance in accordance with Article 28 of the Act is implemented.

Article 5 (Keeping of information on building management) Where a manager has obtained building permission or filed a report on building construction in accordance with Article 11 or 14 of the Building Act for falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 9(1) of the Act and has completed repair or reinforcement works, he or she shall record, keep, and maintain the following information by entering such information into the building life cycle information system under Article 7 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "building life cycle information system") in accordance with Article 10(1) of the Act:
  1. Major drawings including plan drawings, elevation drawings, and section drawings before and after construction, such as repair and reinforcement;
  2. Picture of construction works of main structural members defined in Article 2(1)7 of the Building Act (hereinafter referred to as "main structural member").

CHAPTER Ⅲ BUILDING MANAGEMENT INSPECTION AND MEASURES THEREFOR

Article 6 (Buildings excluded from establishment of building management plans) (1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11(1)5 of the Act means any of the following buildings: <Amended on May 15, 2023>
  1. Factories and knowledge industry centers defined in subparagraphs 1 and 13 of Article 2 of the Industrial Cluster Development and Factory Establishment Act;
  2. Schools defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on the Prevention of and Compensation for Accidents at School;
  3. Detached housing defined in subparagraph 1a of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  4. Other buildings publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as deemed unnecessary to establish building management plans.
  (2) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11(2)8 of the Act means the following:
  1. Matters concerning managers;
  2. Matters deemed necessary for building management, from among certification or evaluation under this Act or relevant statutes and regulations, such as the Green Buildings Construction Support Act.
  (3) "Institution or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 11(7) of the Act means building management support centers designated in accordance with Article 39(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "building management support centers").

Article 7 (Examination of safety of structure of unique buildings) (1) "Building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 12(2) of the Act means the following buildings: <Amended on Dec. 17, 2024>
  1. Buildings of unique structures defined in subparagraph 18 (excluding item c) of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  2. Buildings of flat slab structure (referring to structure consisting of drop panels or columns, without beams).
  (2) Buildings under paragraph (1) shall be inspected by applying the following standards in accordance with Article 12(2) of the Act:
  1. A person with experience and knowledge in structural safety of the building shall conduct an exterior inspection thereof;
  2. A person in charge of inspection under Article 18(3) of the Act shall conduct a preliminary examination on information, etc. on unique structural and structural changes and formulate an inspection plan thereof;
  3. Cracks, damage, etc. of members of a building falling defined in subparagraph 18a or b of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act shall be observed.
  (3) Except as provided in paragraph (2), matters related to tightening or modifying inspection standards of the building shall be prescribed and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as the building management inspection guidelines under Article 17 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "building management inspection guidelines").

Article 8 (Buildings Subject to Regular Inspections) (1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as public-use buildings" in Article 13(1) of the Act means the following buildings; provided, schools defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Act on the Prevention of and Compensation for Accidents at School, multi-family housing subject to compulsory management defined in  Article 2(1)2 of the Multi-family Housing Management Act, superstores and quasi-superstores defined in subparagraphs 3 and 4 of Article 2 of the Distribution Industry Development Act, and multi-family housing on which safety management of small-scale multi-family housing has been conducted within 3 years from the date of conducting a regular inspection in accordance with Article 34(2) of the Multi-Family Housing Management Act shall be excluded:
  1. A building with publicly-used establishments under the Special Act on the Safety Control of Publicly Used Establishments, which is prescribed by ordinance of a Special Self-Governing City, Special Self-Governing Province, or Si/Gun/Gu (referring to an autonomous Gu; hereinafter referred to as "ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu");
  2. A building governed by the Act on Ownership and Management of Condominium Buildings, whose total floor area is more than 3,000 square meters;
  3. A public-use building defined in subparagraph 17 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  4. A quasi-public-use building defined in subparagraph 17-2 of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act, which falls under buildings of unique structures under subparagraph 18 of the same Article.
  (2) The manager of a building subject to a regular inspection under Article 13(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "regular inspection") shall request a building management inspection institution notified of designation in accordance with Article 18(1) of the Act to conduct the inspection.
  (3) "Items prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the site, height and shape, structural safety, structural safety, fire safety, building service, energy and environment-friendly management, crime prevention, and formulation and implementation of a building management plan" in the main clause of Article 13(2) of the Act means the following items:
  1. Site: Whether it complies with Articles 40, 42 through 44, and 47 of the Building Act;
  2. Height and shape: whether it complies with Articles 55, 56, 58, 60, and 61 of the Building Act;
  3. Structural safety:
  a. Whether it complies with Article 48 of the Building Act;
  b. Whether it complies with the matters prescribed by the building management inspection guidelines, such as the exterior of a building and the conditions of its main structural member (limited to the first regular inspection conducted after 20 years from the date of approval for use under Article 22 of the Building Act);
  4. Fire safety: Whether it complies with Articles 49, 50, 50-2, 51, 52, 52-2, and 53 of the Building Act;
  5. Building service: Whether it complies with Articles 62 and 64 of the Building Act;
  6. Energy and environment-friendly management: Whether it complies with Article 65-2 of the Building Act and Articles 15, 15-2, 16, and 17 of the Green Buildings Construction Support Act;
  7. Crime prevention: Whether it complies with Article 53-2 of the Building Act;
  8. 건축물관리계획 : 수립  및  이행이  적합한지  여부
  9. Other items:
  a. Whether the matters under the subparagraphs of Article 20(2) of the Act are implemented;
  b. Whether a building is maintained in accordance with details in the design drawings submitted at the time of filing an application for approval for use under Article 22 of the Building Act;
  c. Whether there exist any matters to be supplemented to strengthen the safety of buildings and to save energy.

Article 9 (Conducting emergency inspections) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 14(1)3 of the Act means the following cases:
  1. Where it is deemed that there is a risk of collapse, fall, etc. of a building due to substandard design or construction, etc.;
  2. Other cases prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu, such as where it is deemed likely to significantly affect the safe use of buildings.
  (2) The items of an inspection under Article 14(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "emergency inspection") shall be classified as follows:
  1. Structural safety: Whether it complies with Article 48 of the Building Act;
  2. Fire safety: Whether it complies with Articles 49, 50, 50-2, 51, 52, 52-2, and 53 of the Building Act;
  3. Other items for which an inspection is deemed necessary to ensure the safety of buildings.
  (3) The manager of a building requested to conduct an emergency inspection in accordance with Article 14(2) of the Act shall request a building management inspection institution notified of designation in accordance with Article 18(1) of the Act to conduct the inspection.

Article 10 (Conducting inspections of small-scale deteriorated buildings) (1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 15(1)4 of the Act means any of the following buildings:
  1. A building within remodeling promotion zones under Article 5(1) of the Building Act and Article 6(1)6a of the Enforcement Decree of the same Act;
  2. A building within a disaster-prevention district under Article 37(1)4 of the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
  3. A building within a prospective improvement zone or an improvement zone released in accordance with Articles 20 and 21 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments;
  4. A building within an area for promotion of urban regeneration defined in Article 2(1)5 of the Special Act on Promotion of and Support for Urban Regeneration;
  5. A building within an area zoned to manage natural disaster risks under Article 12(1) of the Countermeasures against Natural Disasters Act;
  6. A building constructed before the enactment date of the Building Act (January 20, 1962);
  7. Other buildings prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu, such as buildings which are vulnerable to safety risks or at risk of disaster.
  (2) A Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu may designate a building management inspection institution from the list under Article 12(3) and request an inspection under Article 15(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "inspection of small-scale deteriorated buildings, etc."); in such cases, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall notify the building management inspection institution of the following matters:
  1. Use and structure of a building subject to inspection;
  2. Location and scale of a building subject to inspection;
  3. Other reasons why inspections are deemed necessary.
  (3) A building management inspection institution requested to conduct an inspection in accordance with paragraph (2) shall review the actual status of management of the building and determine the timing, methods, etc. of conducting inspections and notify the manager of the relevant building and the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu thereof.

Article 11 (Conducting safety examination) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 16(2)4 of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu deems that an examination under Article 16(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "safety examination") is necessary because it is likely to deteriorate structural safety or fire safety performance due to the occurrence of a disaster, such as earthquake or fire;
  2. Other cases prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) A report on the results under Article 16(5) of the Act shall include the following:
  1. Outline of the safety inspection, such as the outline of the building and the scope and the task details of safety inspection;
  2. Results of collecting and analyzing data, such as design drawings, structural estimates, and repair and reinforcement history;
  3. Results of on-site investigations and tests, such as analysis of findings from exterior investigation and material testing and measurement;
  4. Results of evaluation on building conditions;
  5. Results of safety evaluation such as structural analysis of buildings;
  6. Results of comprehensive evaluation on buildings;
  7. Methods of repair and reinforcement;
  8. Comprehensive results and matters requiring additional supplementation;
  9. Other matters concerning safety inspection, determined by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (3) An institution requested to conduct a safety examination in accordance with Article 16(3) of the Act shall submit a report on the results thereof to the relevant manager, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu in accordance with Article 16(5) of the Act within 30 days from the date it completes the safety examination. In such cases, it may be submitted by entering it into a building life cycle information system.

Article 12 (Designation of building management inspection institution) (1) "Persons ... prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 18(1)5 of the Act means the following persons: <Amended on Dec. 8, 2020>
  1. A person who has registered the establishment of a professional engineer office specializing in the construction field in accordance with Article 6 of the Professional Engineers Act;
  2. The Korea Real Estate Board under the Korea Real Estate Board Act;
  3. The Korea Land and Housing Corporation established under the Korea Land and Housing Corporation Act.
  (2) The requirements to be met by a building management inspection institution shall be as specified in Appendix 1.
  (3) The Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Do Governor, or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor (hereinafter referred to as "Mayor/Do Governor") shall prepare and manage a list of persons under the subparagraphs of Article 18(1) of the Act after making a public announcement on recruitment. In such cases, the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, the Metropolitan City Mayor, or the Do Governor shall consult in advance with the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu.
  (4) in accordance with Article 18(1) of the Act, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall designate a building management inspection institution from the list under paragraph (3) of this Article.
  (5) Matters necessary for the public announcement of recruitment of building management inspection institutions, the list preparation and management, and the designation thereof under paragraphs (3) and (4) may be prescribed by ordinance of the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province.

Article 13 (Qualification of inspectors) (1) A building management inspection institution shall designate a person who meets the qualification standards specified in Appendix 2 as a person in charge of inspection of the relevant building management inspection in accordance with Article 18(3) of the Act.
  (2) A person in charge of inspection designated in accordance with paragraph (1) shall exercise overall control over and supervision over the management and inspection of the relevant building.
  (3) The qualification standards for inspectors under Article 18(4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "inspectors") shall be as specified in Appendix 2.
  (4) Where a person in charge of inspection and an inspector intend to conduct regular inspections, emergency inspections, inspections of small-scale deteriorated buildings, etc., and safety inspections under Articles 13 through 16 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "building management inspection"), he or she shall complete initial education and refresher education in accordance with Appendix 3.
  (5) The considerations for services for building management inspections under Article 18(6) of the Act shall be calculated by classifying them into labor costs, royalties, direct costs, indirect costs, and additional expenses incurred in performing the duties (referring to additional expenses, etc. for structural safety inspections under Article 8(3)3b). In such cases, further details necessary for calculating the considerations for services shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 14 (Reporting on results of building management inspection) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 20(2)8 of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on May 27, 2025>
  1. Safety inspections and safety management of small-scale multi-family housing under Articles 33 and 34 of the Multi-family Housing Management Act;
  2. Regular inspections and non-periodic inspections under Article 17 of the Urban Gas Business Act;
  3. Reconstruction diagnosis under Article 12 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments.

Article 15 (Restrictions on use of building) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 21(1) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where the strength or stiffness (power of resistance to transformation) of the main structural member has been significantly reduced;
  2. Where excessive transformation of the main structural member has occurred or cracks therein have deepened;
  3. Where it is deemed necessary to ensure the safety of buildings bases on the results of implementation of building management inspections.
  (2) Where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu issue an order to take measures, such as restrictions on use, prohibition of use, or dismantlement of the relevant building in accordance with Article 21(3) of the Act, he or she shall notify the manager of the relevant building in writing, including the details of measures taken and reasons therefor.

Article 16 (Implementation of inspection results) (1) "Serious defects prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as seismic performance and fire safety performance" in Article 22(1) of the Act means any of the cases falling under the subparagraphs of Article 15(1):
  (2) Where a manager is required to take necessary measures, such as repair and reinforcement, in accordance with Article 22(1) of the Act, he or she shall formulate a plan for taking measures, such as repair and reinforcement, within 60 days from the date of receipt of the results of a building management inspection in accordance with Article 20(1) of the Act, and report it to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (3) The manager shall commence to take measures in accordance with the plan for measures, such as repair and reinforcement, under paragraph (2) within 2 years from the date he or she receives a report on the results of a building management inspection in accordance with Article 20(1) of the Act. In such cases, he or she shall complete necessary measures, such as repair and reinforcement, within 3 years from the date of commencement, unless there is a compelling reason not to do so.

Article 17 (Evaluation on results of building management inspection) (1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or a Mayor/Do Governor may select the subject matter of evaluation of the results of a building management inspection in consideration of the use, total floor area, number of floors, etc. of a building in accordance with Article 24(1) of the Act. In such cases, the subject matter of evaluation may be selected by the random sampling method in order to conduct a sample survey.
  (2) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport or a Mayor/Do Governor evaluates the results of a building management inspection in accordance with Article 24(1) of the Act, he or she shall notify the following persons of the results of such evaluation:
  1. Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport conducts an evaluation: The Mayor/Do Governor or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu having jurisdiction over an area to which the subject matters of the building management inspection belongs;
  2. Where the Mayor/Do Governor conducts an evaluation: The following persons:
  a. The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport;
  b. The head of a Si/Gun/Gu (excluding cases where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor or a Special Self-Governing Province Governor conducts an evaluation).

Article 18 (Suspension of business of building management inspection institution) The standards for the disposition of the suspension of business under Article 25(1) of the Act, the types of violations subjection to imposition of penalty surcharges, and amounts of penalty surcharges shall be as specified in Appendix 4.

Article 19 (Reinforcement of fire safety performance of buildings) "Requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the total floor area, use, and finishing materials" in the provisions, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 27(2)of the Act means a building that meets all of the following requirements; provided, the requirements under subparagraph 4 shall apply only to subparagraph 1a, c, e, and h:
  1. That it shall be any of the following buildings used for the following purposes:
  a. Public baths and postpartum care centers, from among facilities under subparagraph 3 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  b. Regional children's center, from among facilities under subparagraph 3 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  c. Private teaching institutes and communal living facilities, from among facilities under subparagraph 4 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  d. General hospitals, hospitals, dental clinics, Korean medicine hospitals, mental health hospitals, and isolation hospitals, from among facilities under subparagraph 9 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  e. Private teaching institutes, from among facilities under subparagraph 10 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  f. Children-related facilities, welfare facilities for senior citizens, and social welfare facilities, from among facilities under subparagraph 11 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  g. Juvenile training centers, from among facilities under subparagraph 12 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  h. Communal living facilities, from among facilities under subparagraph 15 of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  2. That it shall be a building built by external insulation method, which is constructed with insulating materials and exterior wall closing materials below the standards of incombustible materials (materials with noncombustible nature);
  3. That it shall be a building in which no sprinkler or basic sprinkler is installed;
  4. That it shall be a building with the total floor area of 1,000 square meters or less, all or part of the first floor of which has a piloti structure and is used as a parking lot.

Article 20 (Support for reinforcement of fire safety performance) (1) The State or local governments shall fully or partially subsidize the following expenses incurred in the reinforcement of fire safety performance of buildings in accordance with Article 29-2(2) of the Act: <Amended on Jul. 11, 2023>
  1. Construction costs or installation costs for the reinforcement of fire safety performance of buildings;
  2. Expenses necessary for design or supervision under relevant statutes or regulations, such as the Building Act, the Certified Architects Act, and the Firefighting System Installation Business Act.
  (2) Deleted. <Jul. 11, 2023>
  [Title Amended on Jul. 11, 2023]

CHAPTER IV DISMANTLEMENT AND DISTRUCTION OF BUILDING SITES

Article 21 (Buildings subject to reporting on dismantlement of buildings) (1) "Buildings prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30(1)3 of the Act means any of the following buildings:
  1. A building under Article 14(1)1 or 3 of the Building Act;
  2. A building with a height of less than 12 meters, which is located in a control area, agricultural and forest area, or natural environment conservation area under the National Land Planning And Utilization Act; in such cases, where a part of the relevant building extends over an urban area under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act, the area to which the majority of the building falls shall apply;
  3. Other buildings prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) A person who intends to file a report in accordance with the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30(1) of the Act shall submit a report prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu (hereafter referred to as "permitting authority" in this Chapter).
  (3) Upon receipt of an application for permission to dismantle a building or a written report on dismantlement of a building in accordance with Article 30(3) of the Act or paragraph (2) of this Article, the permitting authority shall verify whether the building or material used in the building contains asbestos, and shall notify the following persons of the relevant facts without delay, if the building or material contains asbestos: <Amended on Aug. 2, 2022>
  1. The head of a regional employment and labor office who issues an order to take measures in accordance with Article 119(4) of the Occupational Safety and Health Act and subparagraph 33 of Article 115 of the Enforcement Decree of the same Act;
  2. The Mayor/Do Governor, the head of the competent basin environmental office, or the head of a regional environmental office who verifies documents in accordance with Article 17(5) of the Wastes Control Act and Article 37(1)2a and (2) 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the same Act.
  (4) Upon receipt of an application for permission for dismantlement of a building or a report on dismantlement of a building in accordance with Article 30(3) of the Act and paragraph (2) of this Article, the permitting authority shall verify whether the relevant building or the site for such building has gas facilities (including gas pipelines; hereinafter the same shall apply) that have not been subject to safety measures and where there are gas facilities that have not been subject to safety measures, the permitting authority shall notify any of the following persons of such fact without delay: <Added on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. A business entity who owns pipelines outside of the place of business who takes safety measures in accordance with Article 23-6(1) of the High-Pressure Gas Safety Control Act;
  2. An urban gas business entity who takes safety measures in accordance with Article 28-3(2) of the Urban Gas Business Act;
  3. A liquefied petroleum gas filling business entity and a collective supplier of liquefied petroleum gas who take safety measures in accordance with Article 49-7(1) of the Safety Control and Business of Liquefied Petroleum Gas Act.
  (5) "Scope of duties prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as building structure" in Article 30(4)2 and (5)2 of the Act means building structure, building construction, or construction safety, among the scope of duties under Appendix 2-2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Professional Engineers Act. <Amended on Aug. 2, 2022; Jan. 2, 2024>
  (6) "Building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 30(8) of the Act means the following buildings: <Amended on Aug. 2, 2022; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. Buildings of unique structures defined in subparagraph 18b or c of Article 2 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act;
  2. Buildings that are dismantled by placing more than 10 tons of equipment on the building.
  3. Buildings that are dismantled through implosion.

Article 21-2 (Matters of permission for modification of building dismantlement permit or reporting on modification thereof) (1) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the former part of Article 30-3(1) of the Act means any of the following matters:
  1. Dismantlement method;
  2. Order of dismantlement works;
  3. Part to be dismantled and its size;
  4. Types of dismantlement equipment;
  5. Whether the building subject to dismantlement contains asbestos;
  6. Safety management measures at the site of dismantlement works.
  (2) Upon receipt of an application for permission for modification or a reporting on modification under Article 30-3(1) of the Act, the permitting authority shall verify whether the building or material used in the building contains asbestos and shall notify the persons falling under the subparagraphs of Article 21(3) of the relevant facts without delay, if the building or material contains asbestos.
  (3) Upon receipt of an application for permission for modification or a reporting on modification under Article 30-3(1) of the Act, the permitting authority shall verify whether the building or the site for such building has gas facilities that have not been subject to safety measures and shall notify the persons falling under the subparagraphs of Article 21(4) of the relevant facts without delay, if the building or materials has gas facilities that have not been subject to safety measures. <Added on Jan. 2, 2024>
  (4) Upon receipt of an application for permission for modification or a reporting on modification under Article 30-3(1) of the Act and if a building subject to dismantlement falls under the subparagraphs of Article 21(6), the permitting authority shall request the Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety under the Act on the Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety (hereinafter referred to as the "Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety") to review the modified dismantlement plan. <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  (5) "Matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as the change of a dismantling worker" in Article 30-3(2) of the Act means the following matters: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. The scheduled date of the commencement of construction (limited to cases where the date of commencement is modified by at least 30 days);
  2. Dismantling workers, subcontractors, site managers, and construction engineers placed at the site of dismantlement works.
  [This Article Added on Aug. 2, 2022]

Article 21-3 (On-site inspections) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as where the permitting authority receives a report on the commencement of dismantlement works" in Article 30-4(1) of the Act means the following cases: <Amended on Dec. 6, 2022>
  1. Where the permitting authority receives a report on the commencement of dismantlement works under Article 30-2(1) of the Act;
  2. Where the permitting authority intends to verify whether there exists good cause under Article 31(2)3 of the Act;
  3. Where the permitting authority deems it necessary to conduct an on-site inspection in any of the following cases:
  a. Where the permitting authority receives an application for permission for modification or a report on modification under Article 30-3(1) of the Act;
  b. Where the permitting authority receives a report on modification under Article 30-3(2) of the Act;
  c. Where the permitting authority intends to verify whether a supervisor of dismantlement works conscientiously performs his or her duties in accordance with the provisions of Article 32(1) through (3) of the Act;
  d. Where the permitting authority intends to verify whether a dismantling worker faithfully performs his or her duties under the subparagraphs of Article 32-2 of the Act;
  e. Where the permitting authority has received a report, information, etc. on violations, etc. related to dismantlement works of a building;
  4. Where the dismantlement process of a building is prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu to verify whether the dismantlement works of a building is performed in compliance with a dismantlement plan and relevant statutes and regulations when the dismantlement process of a building reaches the hold point under the former part of Article 32(5)1 of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "hold point").
  [This Article Added on Aug. 2, 2022]

Article 22 (Designation of supervisors of dismantlement works of buildings) (1) The Mayor/Do Governor shall prepare and manage a list of persons qualified as supervisor under Article 31(1) of the Act after making a public announcement on recruitment. In such cases, the Special Metropolitan City Mayor, a Metropolitan City Mayor, or a Do Governor shall consult in advance with the head of the competent Si/Gun/Gu.
  (2) The permitting authority shall designate a supervisor of dismantlement works for the following buildings from the list under paragraph (1) in accordance with Article 31(1) of the Act: <Amended on Oct. 28, 2021; Aug. 2, 2022; Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. A building subject to permission for dismantlement under the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30(1) of the Act and paragraph (2) of the same Article;
  2. A building subject to reporting on dismantlement under the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30(1) of the Act and falling under any of the following items:
  a. A building under the subparagraphs of Article 21(6);
  b. A building that the permitting authority deems necessary for safe management of dismantlement works in cases where a building to be dismantled is located in an area crowded with floating population or densely packed with buildings.
  (3) Where a building is dismantled and a new building falling under Article 25(2) of the Building Act is to be constructed, upon request by a manager, the permitting authority may designate a supervisor of dismantlement works designated in accordance with paragraph (2) of this Article as a project supervisor under Article 25(2) of the Building Act. In such cases, the permitting authority shall designate a supervisor of dismantlement works in consideration of the size, use, etc. of the building to be constructed.
  (4) Matters necessary for the preparation and management of a list of supervisors of dismantlement works, and the designation thereof under the provisions of paragraphs (1) through (3) may be prescribed by ordinance of the Special Metropolitan City, Metropolitan City, Special Self-Governing City, Do, or Special Self-Governing Province. <Amended on Aug. 2, 2022>

Article 23 (Replacement of supervisors of dismantlement works) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 31(2)4 of the Act means the following cases: <Amended on Aug. 2, 2022>
  1. Where the supervisor of dismantlement works does not qualify for the supervision of dismantlement works;
  2. Where the supervisor of dismantlement works has performed duties in violation of Article 32 of the Act by intent or gross negligence;
  3. Where the supervisor of dismantlement works refuses or fails to conduct the supervision of dismantlement works without good cause;
  4. Other cases prescribed by ordinance of a Si/Gun/Gu, where the supervisor of dismantlement works is unable to continue to perform his or her duties or is inappropriate to perform such duties.

Article 23-2 (Standards for placement of construction inspectors of dismantlement works of buildings) (1) "Building prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 31(3) of the Act means the following buildings: <Amended on Jan. 2, 2024>
  1. A building subject to permission for dismantlement under the main clause, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30(1) of the Act and paragraph (2) of the same Article;
  2. A building subject to reporting on dismantlement under the proviso, with the exception of the subparagraphs, of Article 30(1) of the Act and falling under any of the subparagraphs of Article 21(6).
  (2) "Person with qualifications or experience prescribed by Presidential Decree" in the proviso of Article 31(3) of the Act means a person who is not a contractor himself or herself or does not belong to an affiliate company of the contractor (referring to an affiliate company defined in subparagraph 12 of Article 2 of the Monopoly Regulation and Fair Trade Act), falling under the following classifications:
  1. Where a construction inspector is placed at a hold point: A person falling under the following items:
  a. A certified architect defined in subparagraph 1 of Article 2 of the Certified Architects Act;
  b. A person, as a principal engineer, who is qualified to perform construction project management under Article 39 of the Construction Technology Promotion Act;
  2. Where a construction inspector is placed in the dismantlement process, other than at a hold point: A person falling under the following items:
  a. A person under each item of subparagraph 1;
  b. An assistant architect defined in subparagraph 2 of Article 2 of the Certified Architects Act;
  c. A person who belongs to a professional engineering office under Article 6 of the Professional Engineers Act or a construction engineering business entity, etc. under the subparagraphs of Article 23(9) of the Certified Architects Act, falling under any of the following subitems:
  1) A person who obtains a national technical qualification in the field of construction under the National Technical Qualifications Act;
  2) A person who is qualified to perform construction project management under Article 39 of the Construction Technology Promotion Act and whose occupational field is construction under subparagraph 3d of Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the same Act.
  (3) Standards for the placement of construction inspectors under the former part of Article 31(6) of the Act shall include the following details:
  1. In cases of dismantlement works of buildings under paragraph (1)1, a construction inspector shall be placed in accordance with the following classifications:
  a. A building with the total floor area of less than 3,000 square meters: At least 1 person;
  b. A building with the total floor area of more than 3,000 square meters: At least 2 persons; provided, where the permitting authority deems unnecessary to place more than 2 construction inspectors in consideration of the difficulty of dismantlement works, the part and size of area to be dismantled, etc. at the request of the manager, 1 person may be placed;
  2. In cases of dismantlement works of buildings under paragraph (1)2, at least 1 construction inspector shall be placed;
  3. In cases of reaching a hold point in the process of dismantlement works, a construction inspector shall be placed in accordance with the following items:
  a. The placement period shall last until the next stage of the dismantlement process proceeds;
  b. In cases of placing construction inspectors in accordance with the main clause or the proviso of subparagraph 1b, a person falling under paragraph 2(1) shall be at least 1 person;
  c. Where there is a person falling under paragraph 2(1) among the persons belonging to the supervisor of dismantlement works, the relevant person (including a construction inspector falling under the same subparagraph who is placed in the dismantlement process, other than at a hold point) shall be placed.
  [This Article Wholly Amended on Dec. 6, 2022]

Article 23-3 (Designation of educational institution for dismantlement works) (1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may designate an educational institution for dismantlement works (hereinafter referred to as "educational institution for dismantlement works"), from among the following institutions or organizations, in accordance with Article 31-2(2) of the Act:
  1. The Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety;
  2. The Korea Institute of Registered Architects under Article 31 of the Certified Architects Act;
  3. The Professional Engineers Association under Article 14 of the Building Act;
  4. A specialized educational institution in the field of safety management or construction project management among the educational institutions designated and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in accordance with the former part of Article 43(2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Construction Technology Promotion Act.
  5. Other institutions or organizations recognized by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport as having expertise in the supervision of dismantlement works of buildings and the preparation and examination of a dismantlement plan.
  (2) Standards for the designation of educational institutions for dismantlement works shall be as follows:
  1. Its curriculum and educational content shall be appropriate to improve the quality of a supervisor of dismantlement works, construction inspector, and persons who prepare and examine dismantlement plans;
  2. It shall have at least 1 faculty member per educational subject;
  3. It shall have lecture facilities and equipment necessary for education;
  4. It shall have the ability to raise operating expenses.
  (3) An institution or organization which intends to be designated as an educational institution of dismantlement works shall submit an application for designation prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied with the documents stating the following details, to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport:
  1. An operational plan including the curriculum and educational content;
  2. The current status on securing faculty members;
  3. The current status on securing facilities and equipment necessary for education;
  4. A plan for raising operating expenses.
  (4) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport designates an educational institution for dismantlement works, he or she shall issue a certificate of designation prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport to the designated person, and publicly notify the name, representative, location, etc. of the educational institution for dismantlement works in the Official Gazette.
  (5) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (4), matters necessary for the designation, etc. of an educational institution for dismantlement works shall be prescribed by Presidential Decree.
  [This Article Added on Aug. 2, 2022]

Article 23-4 (Detailed standards for hold points) (1) The detailed standards for hold points in the former part of Article 32(5)1 of the Act shall be as follows:
  1. Before the commencement of dismantlement process of finishing materials;
  2. Before the commencement of dismantlement process of roofs;
  3. Before the commencement of dismantlement process of the middle floor;
  4. Before the commencement of dismantlement process of the underground floor.
  (2) Necessary matters concerning the specific timing of hold points under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  [This Article Added on Aug. 2, 2022]

CHAPTER Ⅴ  SUPPORT FOR BUILDING MANAGEMENT

Article 24 (Conclusion of agreements for research and development projects for building management technology) (1) "Institution or organization prescribed by Presidential Decree" under Article 35(1) of the Act means the following Institution or organization: <Amended on Oct. 19, 2021; Jan. 27, 2026>
  1. National and public research institutes;
  2. Schools defined in Article 2 of the Higher Education Act;
  3. Professional research business operators reported in accordance with Article 6(1) of the Research Industry Promotion Act;
  4. Business-affiliated research institutes or departments solely responsible for research and development recognized in accordance with Article 7(1) of the Act on Support for Research and Development of Business-Affiliated Research Institutes;
  5. Research Institutes which are corporations established in accordance with the Civil Act or any other statute;
  6. Industrial technology research cooperatives under the Industrial Technology Research Cooperatives Support Act;
  7. A government-funded research institute or government-funded science and technology research institutes established in accordance with the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Research Institutes or the Act on the Establishment, Operation and Fostering of Government-Funded Science and Technology Research Institutes;
  8. Specific research institutes under the Specific Research Institutes Support Act.
  (2) Where the head of a central administrative agency selects a research and development task of building management technology, he or she shall conclude an agreement on the research and development project of building management technology (hereinafter referred to as "agreement") with an institution or organization that performs and manages research and development in the relevant field (hereinafter referred to as "main research institute"), from among the institutions or organizations under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).
  (3) When the head of a main research institute conducts a research and development project in accordance with paragraph (2), where technology development expenses under Article 35(2) of the Act (including expenses in kind; hereafter the same shall apply in this paragraph) are included in the research and development expenses, he or she shall conclude an investment contract or research contract with a person who bears such technology development expenses in advance.
  (4) An agreement shall include the following matters:
  1. The plan for research and development projects;
  2. Deleted; <Dec. 29, 2020>
  3. Matters concerning payment methods of research and development expenses and use and management thereof;
  4. Matters concerning reporting on research and development results;
  5. Matters concerning the attribution and utilization of research and development results;
  6. Matters concerning the collection and utilization of royalties;
  7. Matters concerning the evaluation on research and development results;
  8. Matters concerning the modification and termination of agreements;
  9. Matters concerning measures taken against violations of agreements;
  10. Other matters necessary for research and development.
  (5) Where deemed necessary, the head of a main research institute may entrust part of the relevant research task to an institution or organization under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).

Article 25 (Contributions for research and development projects for building management technology) (1) Contributions under Article 35(2) of the Act shall be paid in installments; provided, it may be paid in a lump sum if deemed necessary in consideration of the scale, timing of commencement, etc. of the research task.
  (2) Where the head of a main research institute receives expenses incurred in conducting a project for research and development of building management technology (hereinafter referred to as "research and development expenses") in accordance with Article 35(2) of the Act, he or she shall establish and manage a separate account.
  (3) The head of a main research institute shall use research and development expenses from the following expenses, as determined and publicly notified by the head of a central administrative agency that has entered into an agreement (hereinafter referred to as "head of a managing central administrative agency"):
  1. Labor costs for researchers;
  2. Direct costs: Expenses for research equipment and facilities, material costs, computer processing and management costs, prototype production costs, travel expenses, expenses for daily necessities and charges, expenses for technical information-related activities, and expenses for research activities;
  3. Indirect costs: Indirect expenses, research and development reserves, expenses for applying for and registering intellectual property rights, expenses for scientific and cultural activities, and expenses for safety management of laboratories;
  4. Expenses for commissioned research and development.
  (4) The head of a main research institute shall report the results of use of research and development expenses according to the following documents to the head of the competent central administrative agency within 90 days after the end of the agreement period:
  1. A report on the plan to use expenses for research and development and the results of execution thereof;
  2. Documents, such as a written opinion on the accounting audit, related to the execution of expenses for research and development determined and publicly notified by the head of the competent central administrative institute.
  (5) The head of a main research institute may, upon request by a business entity, etc. related to building management under Article 37 of the Act, allow him or her to use the results of research and development projects on building management technology in the production process. In such cases, when the use of such results in obtaining the effects of cost reduction, quality improvement, etc., the head of the main research institute may collect royalties prescribed in the agreement from such users.
  (6) When the head of a main research institute collects royalties in accordance with paragraph (5), he or she shall report such fact to the head of the competent central administrative agency within 30 days from the date of collection.
  (7) The head of a main research institute shall use royalties collected in accordance with paragraph (5) for the purposes of raising, etc. research and development expenses for research and development and basic research, as publicly notified by the head of the competent central administrative agency, and shall report the results of use of such royalties for the relevant year to the head of the competent central administrative agency by March 31 of the following year.

Article 26 (Implementation of pilot project for building management) (1) The head of a central administrative agency shall formulate a plan for pilot project including the following matters to conduct a pilot project for promoting the building management under Article 35(3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "pilot project"):
  1. Matters concerning the objective and strategy of the pilot project and promotional system thereof;
  2. Matters concerning building management technology to be applied to the pilot project;
  3. Matters concerning raising funds necessary for the plot project.
  (2) The head a central administrative agency may designate a project and area eligible for conducting a pilot project (hereinafter referred to as "eligible pilot project") at the request of an institution that conducts research and development projects for building management technology (hereinafter referred to as "research institute for building management technology") in accordance with Article 35(1) of the Act.
  (3) An eligible pilot project shall meet all of the following criteria:
  1. The objectives of the pilot project shall be attainable;
  2. Fund-raising plans for the pilot project shall be appropriate and feasible;
  3. The pilot project shall be implemented swiftly.
  (4) Where a research institute for building management technology intends to request the designation of an eligible pilot project in accordance with paragraph (2), it shall submit the following documents to the head of the relevant central administrative agency:
  1. A plan for the pilot project containing the details under the subparagraphs of paragraph (3);
  2. Documents concerning budget, human resources, etc. that the institution which has filed for application can support for an eligible pilot project.
  (5) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (4), matters necessary for conducting pilot projects shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 27 (Fostering of engineers for building management) (1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may investigate the current status, etc. of education and training of engineers on building management to formulate and implement policies under Article 36(1) of the Act.
  (2) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may conduct education and training containing the following matters in accordance with Article 36(1) of the Act:
  1. Matters concerning the formulation and implementation of building management plans;
  2. Matters concerning maintenance of structural safety and fire safety performance of buildings;
  3. Other matters that the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport deems necessary for education and training.
  (3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may require a building management support center to conduct education and training for engineers on building management in accordance with Article 36(2) of the Act.
  (4) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may determine and publicly notify detailed matters concerning the details, methods, etc. of education and training of engineers on building management.

Article 28 (Support for business operators related to building management) (1) The head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government may provide administrative or financial support to the following person in accordance with Article 37(1) of the Act: <Amended on Sep. 14, 2021>
  1. A construction engineering business entity under subparagraph 9 of Article 2 of the Construction Technology Promotion Act;
  2. A person who has filed a report on the establishment of an architectural firm under Article 23(1) of the Certified Architects Act;
  3. A person who has registered the establishment of a professional engineer office specializing in the construction field in accordance with Article 6 of the Professional Engineers Act;
  4. An institution specializing in safety examinations registered in accordance with Article 28(1) of the Special Act on the Safety Control and Maintenance of Establishments.
  (2) Where the head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government intends to provide support in accordance with Article 37(1) of the Act, it shall determine the details, procedures, etc. for support and publicly announce such fact in the Official Gazette or official report and on the website for a period of at least 30 days.
  (3) The head of a central administrative agency or the head of a local government may provide necessary support by designating the exemplary business operators for building management, from among the persons falling under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1).

Article 29 (Designation of building management support centers) (1) "Public institution prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 39(1)6 of the Act means public institutions under Article 4 of the Act on the Management of Public Institutions, having all the following matters:
  1. A dedicated organization to provide support for building management and its budget and facilities;
  2. At least 10 professional human resources to provide support for building management;
  3. Operational regulations for providing support for building management.
  (2) A person who intends to be designated as an a building management support center shall submit an application for designation prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, accompanied with the following documents, to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport in accordance with Article 39(1) of the Act:
  1. Operating plans for building management support centers;
  2. Current status on securing human resources, organization, and facilities for building management support centers;
  3. Budget-financing plans to operate building management support centers.
  (3) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to designate a person who files an application as a building management support center in accordance with paragraph (2), he or she shall issue a written designation prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Agriculture, Food and Rural Affairs.
  (4) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may request a building management support center to perform the following duties: <Amended on Jul. 11, 2023>
  1. Fact-finding surveys under Article 6;
  2. Assistance to support for reinforcement of fire safety performance under Article 29-2 of the Act;
  3. Promotion of projects to facilitate international cooperation and overseas expansion of building management technology under Article 38 of the Act.
  (5) Building management support centers under paragraph (1) shall submit the following documents to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport by the date classified as follows:
  1. Business plans: By the end of February of each year;
  2. Performance results of the duties for the previous year: By March 31 of the following year.
  (6) Where building management support centers fall under the following cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may revoke the designation of the management support center; provided, such designation shall be revoked in the case of subparagraph 1:
  1. Where it obtains designation as building management support centers by fraud or other improper means;
  2. Where it fails to continuously perform the duties of building management support centers for at least 6 months from the date of designation without good cause;
  3. Where it is unable to perform the duties of building management support centers.
  (7) Where the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport intends to revoke the designation thereof in accordance with paragraph (6), it shall hold a hearing.

CHAPTER VI SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS

Article 30 (Corrective orders for buildings) (1) "Cases prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 41(1)3 of the Act means buildings determined to impede in the establishment of public facilities, such as roadways, as a result of deliberation by a local building committee under Article 5-5 of the Enforcement Decree of the Building Act.
  (2) Where the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to pay reasonable compensation in accordance with Article 41(3) of the Act, he or she shall pay a compensation for possible losses which may be incurred by taking measures under paragraph (1) of the same Article at the market price.
  (3) Where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu fails to reach an agreement on the amount of compensation under paragraph (2) with the owner of the relevant building, he or she shall pay or deposit the amount of compensation and notify the owner of the relevant building of such fact. In such cases, if the owner consents thereto, he or she may be notified by electronic document.
  (4) A person dissatisfied with the payment or the deposit of compensation in accordance with paragraph (3) may file an application for adjudication with the competent land expropriation commission under Article 51 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land for Public Works Projects within 20 days from the date he or she is notified of the payment or the deposit in accordance with paragraph (3).
  (5) The provisions of Articles 83 through 86 of the Act on Acquisition of and Compensation for Land for Public Works Projects shall apply mutatis mutandis to the adjudication under paragraph (4).

Article 31 (Procedures for improvement of unoccupied buildings) (1) Where a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu intends to dismantle an unoccupied building under Article 42(1) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "unoccupied building") ex officio in accordance with Article 43(1) of the Act, he or she shall notify the owner of the unoccupied building of the grounds for dismantlement, the scheduled date of dismantlement, etc. by no later than 7 days before the scheduled date of dismantlement, in accordance with a notice of dismantlement prescribed by Decree of the Ministry of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (2) The Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall pay the arithmetic mean of the amount appraised by at least 2 appraisal corporations, etc. under the Act on Appraisal and Certified Appraisers (including 1 appraisal corporation, etc. recommended in accordance with the main clause of paragraph (3)) to the owners of unoccupied buildings as compensation in accordance with Article 43(3) of the Act. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2022>
  (3) The owner of an unoccupied building shall recommend 1 appraisal corporation, etc. to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu within 14 days from the date he or she becomes aware of the decision to dismantle such building ex officio in accordance with paragraph (1); provided, this shall not apply where the whereabouts of the owner of the unoccupied building is unknown or where the owner of the unoccupied building fails to recommend an appraisal corporation, etc. within the period specified in the main clause. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2022>
  (4) The amount of compensation under paragraph (2) shall be calculated based on the date of notification by a Special Self-Governing City Mayor, a Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu in accordance with paragraph (1) or the date of public announcement in accordance with Article 43(2) of the Act.
  (5) Except as provided in paragraphs (2) and (3), matters necessary for the procedure for and method of selecting appraisal corporations shall be prescribed by ordinance of the relevant Si/Gun/Gu. <Amended on Jan. 21, 2022>

Article 32 (Accident investigation) (1) "Where an accident exceeds the scale prescribed by Presidential Decree occurs" in Article 46(1) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Where reconstruction, etc. of a building is needed due to collapse or fall thereof;
  2. Where an accident occurs involving at least 1 death or missing person or at least 5 injured persons.
  (2) "Building which has caused a greater loss than that prescribed by Presidential Decree" in Article 46(4) of the Act means any of the following cases:
  1. Buildings falling under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1);
  2. Other buildings deemed necessary by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport for the prevention of building accidents.

Article 33 (Composition and organization of central building accident investigation committee) (1) The central building accident investigation committee under Article 46(4) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "central building accident investigation committee") shall be comprised of not more than 12 members, including 1 chairperson, in consideration of gender, and the chairperson shall be appointed or commissioned by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among the members.
  (2) Members of the central building accident investigation committee (hereinafter referred to as "investigating member") shall be appointed or commissioned by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport from among the following persons:
  1. A public official of Grade IV or higher related to the duties of building management who has performed such duties for at least 2 years as a public official of Grade IV or higher in charge of building management;
  2. A person who has been holding or has held the position of associate professor or higher in the field of building management in a university for at least 5 years;
  3. A person who is at least a principal grade construction engineer in the field of civil engineering, architecture, or safety management under Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Engineering Technology Promotion Act and has been working or has worked for at least 10 years in the field of building management;
  4. Other persons with extensive knowledge or experience in building management.
  (3) The term of office of an investigating member shall be until the date he or she submits a report on the results of an accident investigation under Article 36(1).
  (4) A meeting of the central building accident investigation committee shall be convened by the chairperson and constitute a quorum, and any decision thereof shall require the consent of a majority of all its incumbent members.
  (5) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (4), matters necessary for the organization, operation, etc. of the central building accident investigation committee shall be determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 34 (Exclusion, challenge, and abstention of investigating members) (1) Where an investigating member appointed or commissioned in accordance with Article 33(2) falls under any of the following, he or she shall be excluded from deliberation and resolution of the agenda concerned:
  1. Where an investigating member or his or her current or former spouse becomes a party (where a party is a corporation, organization, etc., including an executive officer thereof; hereafter the same shall apply in this subparagraph and subparagraph 2) or an interested person (hereafter referred to as the "party" in this paragraph) to the relevant item on agenda, or is a joint holder or joint obligor of a party to the item on agenda;
  2. Where an investigating member is or was a relative of a party to the relevant agenda under Article 777 of the Civil Act;
  3. Where an investigating member has given any testimony, statement, advice, or conducted any research, service (including any subcontract; hereafter the same shall apply in this Article), appraisal, or examination with respect to the relevant agenda item;
  4. Where an investigating member or a corporation or organization, etc. to which the investigating member belongs is or was an agent of any party to the relevant case;
  5. Where any corporation, etc. where an investigating member holds or held a post as an executive or employee within recent 3 years has given any advice, or conducted any research, service, appraisal, or examination with respect to the relevant agenda item.
  (2) If there exists any ground for which it would be difficult to expect the impartial deliberation and resolution of an investigating member, a party to the relevant agenda may file a request for the challenge to him or her with the central building accident investigation committee, and the central building accident investigation committee shall make a decision on such request by its resolution. In such cases, the investigating member subjected to such request for challenge shall not participate in the resolution.
  (3) Where an investigating member finds that any of the grounds for disqualification under paragraph (1) is applicable to him or her, he or she shall voluntarily refrain from the proceedings of deliberation and resolution of the relevant case.
  (4) Where an investigating member falls under any of the following cases, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport may dismiss him or her:
  1. Where the investigating member is unable to continue to perform his or her duties due to a mental disorder, etc.;
  2. Where the investigating member has conducted any irregularity related to his or her duties, such as divulging any information learned in the course of performing activities of the central building accident investigation committee to any third person or using such information for his or her own benefit;
  3. Where it is deemed inappropriate for the investigating member to remain in office to neglect of duties, loss of dignity, or similar ground;
  4. Where the investigating member fails to file an application for abstention even though he or she falls under the subparagraphs of paragraph (1);
  5. Where the member voluntarily expresses his or her intention that it is impracticable to perform his or her duties.

Article 35 (Composition and organization of building accident investigation committee) `Articles 33 and 34 shall apply mutatis mutandis to the organization and operation of the building accident investigation committee under Article 46(5) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as the "building accident investigation committee"). In such cases, "central building accident investigation committee" shall be construed as "building accident investigation committee", "Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport" as "Special Self-Governing City Mayor, Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu," "investigating member" as "member of a building accident investigation committee," and "report on the results of an accident investigation under Article 36(1)" as "report on the results of an accident investigation under Article 36(2)."

Article 36 (Reporting on results of accident investigation) (1) The central building accident investigation committee shall submit a report of the results of accident investigation containing the following matters to the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport within 30 days from the date the accident investigation is completed:
  1. Overview of the accident;
  2. Analysis of causes of the accident;
  3. Results of measures taken and follow-up measures;
  4. Other matters investigated or analyzed in relation to the accident.
  (2) The building accident investigation committee shall submit a report of the results of accident investigation containing the matters in the subparagraphs of paragraph (1) to the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu within 30 days from the date the accident investigation is completed.
  (3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, the Special Self-Governing City Mayor, the Special Self-Governing Province Governor, or the head of a Si/Gun/Gu shall distribute the report on the results of the accident investigation submitted in accordance with paragraphs (1) and (2) to related agencies so that it can be utilized as data for the prevention of similar accidents.

Article 37 (Entrustment of authority) (1) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall entrust the following authorities in accordance with the relevant classifications in accordance with Article 50(2) of the Act: <Amended on Dec. 1, 2020; Jul. 26, 2022; Aug. 2, 2022>
  1. Authority under Article 50(2)1 of the Act: Institutions determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, which are equipped with human resources and equipment necessary for the management and operation of the building life cycle information system;
  2. Authority under Article 50(2)2 of the Act: Institutions under the following items:
  a. Educational institutions under Article 43(2) of the Enforcement Decree of the Construction Technology Promotion Act;
  b. The Korea Institute of Registered Architects under Article 31 of the Certified Architects Act;
  c. The Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety;
  d. Other institutions determined and publicly notified by the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport, which are equipped with human resources and equipment necessary for conducting education for the implementation of building management inspections;
  3. Authority under Article 50(2)3 of the Act: The Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety;
  4. Authority under Article 50(2)4 of the Act: The building management support centers;
  5. Authority under Article 50(2)5 of the Act: The Korea Authority of Land and Infrastructure Safety.
  (2) The head of an institution entrusted with the authority of evaluating the results of the implementation of building management inspections in accordance with paragraph (1)3 (hereinafter referred to as "head of evaluation institution of implementation results") shall determine the detailed matters concerning subjects, methods, etc. of evaluation and obtain approval thereon from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.
  (3) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall publicly notify the matters approved in accordance with paragraph (2).

Article 38 (Evaluation committee for building management inspections) (1) An evaluation committee for building management inspections under Article 50(3) of the Act (hereinafter referred to as "evaluation committee") shall be comprised of up to 300 members, including 1 chairperson and 1 vice chairperson, considering gender composition.
  (2) The head of the evaluation institution of implementation results shall commission members of the evaluation committee by obtaining approval from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport and shall commission its chairperson and vice chairperson from the members of the evaluation committee:
  1. A public official of Grade IV or higher related to the duties of building management who has performed such duties for at least 2 years as a public official of Grade IV or higher in charge of building management;
  2. A person who has been holding or has held the position of associate professor or higher in the field of building management in a university for at least 5 years;
  3. A person who is at least a principal grade construction engineer in the field of civil engineering, architecture, or safety management under Appendix 1 of the Enforcement Decree of the Engineering Technology Promotion Act and has been working or has worked for at least 10 years in the field of building management;
  4. Other persons with extensive knowledge or experience in building management.
  (3) The term of office of a non-public official member, among the chairperson, vice chairperson, and members of an evaluation committee, shall be 2 years, which may be renewed only 1 further term.
  (4) Meetings of the evaluation committee shall be comprised of at least 3 but not more than 7 members, including the chairperson and members designated by the chairperson at each meeting.
  (5) A majority of the members of the evaluation committee under paragraph (4) shall constitute a quorum, and any decision thereof shall require the concurring vote of a majority of those present.
  (6) Article 34 shall apply mutatis mutandis to exclusion of, challenge to, and recusal and dismissal of members of the evaluation committee. In such cases, "central building accident investigation committee" shall be construed as "evaluation committee", "investigating member" as "members of the evaluation committee", and "Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport" as "head of evaluation institution of implementation results".
  (7) Except as provided in paragraphs (1) through (6), the head of the evaluation institution of implementation results shall determine matters necessary for the organization, operation, etc. of the evaluation committee by obtaining approval from the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport.

Article 39 (Processing of personally identifiable information) Where it is inevitable to conduct the following affairs, the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport (including a person to whom authority and affairs of the Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport has been delegated and entrusted in accordance with Articles 11(7) and 50 of the Act) may process data including resident registration numbers under subparagraph 1 of Article 19 of the Enforcement Decree of the Personal Information Protection Act or alien registration numbers under subparagraph 4 of the aforesaid Article:
  1. Affairs related to building management plans under Article 11 of the Act;
  2. Affairs related to regular inspections under Article 13 of the Act;
  3. Affairs related to emergency inspections under Article 14 of the Act;
  4. Affairs related to inspections of small-scale deteriorated buildings, etc. under Article 15 of the Act;
  5. Affairs related to safety examination under Article 16 of the Act.

Article 39-2 (Re-examination of regulation) The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall examine the appropriateness of the placement of construction inspectors under Article 23-2 every 3 years, counting from January 1, 2016 (referring to the period that ends on the day before January 1 of the every third year) and shall take measures, such as making improvements. <Amended on Mar. 24, 2026>
